A||N||2||KRMFiero||Anyone have any tips/tricks to install clutch into 4cyl-5speed?||||1||
Z||000000||KRMFiero||07-05-2001||08:40 PM||||Alright as some of you might remeber My clutch went in my 1985 Iron Duke SE /w 5 speed.<BR>I want to be able to fix it so i can go to kick hill with it, i think i need new clutch fork and thrust baring also, I have never installed a clutch in anything before so any advise would be useful, the clutch I will be using will be a Autozone Replacement one (Its only $150, anyone have any trouble with these?)<P>Kyle<P>------------------<BR>1984 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (Red) Caddy 4.5 Project<BR>1985 Pontiac Fiero 2M4 SE (White)<P>       <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/~Physcokyle/sig2.jpg"> <BR>AOL: Physcokyle||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||07-05-2001||11:38 PM||||Hey Kyle!<BR>Drop the rear of the cradle, separate and remove the pressure plate, clutch and flywheel...<BR>Have the flywheel turned before installing the new clutch and pressure plate...<BR>If you buy the kit, it should have a throwout bearing, but double check...||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||07-06-2001||11:29 AM||||That clutch should be alright. It should come with the TO bearing. Your clutch fork should be fine. Just look at it when you get everything apart.<P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
